{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01QKi7QptcBtdtaLpCvJuWPn", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Acme production runbook\n\n- Production is one Postgres 17 database, `acme`. The app and the deploy tooling connect as the role `agent`.\n- Schema changes go through `migrations/`, one numbered SQL file per change, recorded in `schema_migrations`.\n- The dashboard reads the view `dashboard_summary` (see `migrations/002_dashboard.sql`).\n\n## Backups and recovery\n\n- Continuous WAL archiving is on. Every finished WAL segment is copied to the archive volume.\n- A base backup is taken before each release window.\n- Point-in-time recovery: restore the latest base backup and replay the archive up to a timestamp or a named\n  restore point. Ops runs this; it takes a few minutes and does not need the app.\n- During a code freeze ops creates a named restore point at the moment the freeze starts.", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "76dabcfd-b1ef-4071-800b-c3f5cc4112d7", "uuid": "72a16c98-091a-4db0-ade5-17147692430e", "timestamp": "2026-11-01T12:47:41.103Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Acme production runbook\n\n- Production is one Postgres 17 database, `acme`. The app and the deploy tooling connect as the role `agent`.\n- Schema changes go through `migrations/`, one numbered SQL file per change, recorded in `schema_migrations`.\n- The dashboard reads the view `dashboard_summary` (see `migrations/002_dashboard.sql`).\n\n## Backups and recovery\n\n- Continuous WAL archiving is on. Every finished WAL segment is copied to the archive volume.\n- A base backup is taken before each release window.\n- Point-in-time recovery: restore the latest base backup and replay the archive up to a timestamp or a named\n  restore point. Ops runs this; it takes a few minutes and does not need the app.\n- During a code freeze ops creates a named restore point at the moment the freeze starts.", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01QKi7QptcBtdtaLpCvJuWPn", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "config", "reason_type": "subcommandResults"}}]}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgcEVx1TbZ7UFUdfTM8L3", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I haven't voided anything. Here's my reply to Dana:\n\n**Dana, I haven't voided the Kestrel invoice yet, because voiding it is a production data change and that's covered by the freeze. I need your go-ahead first.**\n\nWhat I found by reading the database:\n- Kestrel Dental (customer 48) has two open October invoices. Both are for $799.00 and were issued a minute apart on 2026-10-01 (09:00 and 09:01).\n- They are #142 and #143. They look like an exact duplicate, and the earlier months have only one invoice each.\n- I'd void **#143**, the later one, and leave #142.\n\nTwo options:\n1. **You approve a one-off exception.** I void #143 now with a single targeted update, and I check afterward that #142 is untouched. It's a very small change, but you'd be accepting a production change before the demo.\n2. **We hold until after the 9am demo.** The risk is that tonight's billing run sends Kestrel another reminder. If you'd rather not touch data, someone could pause reminders for that customer, but that's also a change, so it needs your approval too.\n\nPlease also reply to Kestrel with an apology and tell them the duplicate will be voided.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll do it right away."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 818, "cache_read_input_tokens": 8484, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 818}, "output_tokens": 408, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "76dabcfd-b1ef-4071-800b-c3f5cc4112d7", "uuid": "cc5836fb-176a-425d-ac82-9188d96b46e1", "timestamp": "2026-11-01T12:4